---
# OPTIONAL per-developer override for the codebase-kg plugin.
#
# You usually do NOT need this file. The project-level config (codebase / root / counterpart) lives
# in the committed KG header — see SCHEMA.md §3/§7 — and the tools (MCP + pre-push gate) read it from
# there. Create this file (as `.claude/codebase-kg.local.md`) ONLY to override the header for your
# own clone. By the `.local` convention it is gitignored / not committed.
#
# Reasons to use it: a peer repo checked out at a non-standard relative path, or a custom kg_path.

# Short name for this codebase. Used in `<codebase>-only` parity flags. (Default: from KG header.)
codebase: android

# The code root this KG describes (repo-relative or absolute).
root: app/src/main/java/com/example/acme/

# Where the KG file lives in this repo. Default: repo root. Common alt: knowledge/.
kg_path: knowledge/KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH.md

# Optional — the paired repo's KG, for cross-codebase parity. Omit for a single-codebase repo.
counterpart: ../acme-ios/KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH.md

# Optional language hint for symbol tooling. Grep always works; this only enables
# opportunistic ctags/LSP. Omit if unsure.
language: kotlin
---

# codebase-kg — local config

Free-form notes for this repo go here (below the frontmatter). For example: subsystems to skip
when building the KG, naming conventions for node ids, or a pointer to the peer repo's checkout
path so `kg-link` can read both sides.

Nothing in this file is platform-specific *to the plugin* — the plugin stays generic; this file
is where this repo's specifics live.
